<details class="save-walkthrough">
  <summary>Walk through a save</summary>
  <p class="intro">With the default disk buffer and balanced durability. Illustrative steps, not measured timings.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <div class="step-title">Write returns <span>May still be pending</span></div>
      <p>Your application can read the updated file. The write returning does not establish an explicit save boundary.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="step-title">Synchronize successfully <span>Save boundary</span></div>
      <p>Call <code>syncSync()</code> in the worker, or await <code>volume.sync()</code> through the worker client. This synchronizes the volume's pending data and metadata.</p>
      <p class="failure">If synchronization fails, report the error. Do not show the work as saved.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="step-title">Close and reopen <span>Resume locally</span></div>
      <p>Successfully await <code>closeVfs()</code>. Reopen the same volume in the same browser and origin, then await <code>ready</code> before reading the saved files.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p class="footnote">New writes after synchronization need another save boundary. Local storage can still be cleared or evicted. Export important work as a backup.</p>
</details>

